<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  `foray-notify`'s library manifest (issue #761; PQ-29). AGP merges it into the
  generated app's manifest only once mobile/package.json declares the plugin
  (PQ-30); until then no shell includes the module and nothing here ships.

  POST_NOTIFICATIONS: from Android 13 (API 33) a notification the user has not
  permitted is not shown, and Capacitor refuses to request a permission alias
  whose permission the manifest does not declare. foray-audio declares the same
  permission for its playback notification; the merger keeps one.

  INTERNET is the app's already (Capacitor's template); the check asks the same
  endpoint the show page does, so nothing new is reached.

  WorkManager's own library manifest (androidx.work:work-runtime) brings its
  InitializationProvider, its job service and receivers, and the
  RECEIVE_BOOT_COMPLETED, WAKE_LOCK, ACCESS_NETWORK_STATE and FOREGROUND_SERVICE
  permissions with it. Those merge only when PQ-30 declares the plugin; that PR
  is where the store's permission list and data-safety answers are re-read.
-->
<manifest xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android">
    <uses-permission android:name="android.permission.POST_NOTIFICATIONS" />
    <application>
    </application>
</manifest>
